---
/** Method: the documents, how each figure is built, a worked example, the limits. Figures from the kit. */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { KIT as K } from '../../lib/kit';
import { src, table, others } from '../../lib/helpers';
import { VALUE } from '../../content/home';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('method', lang);
const title = 'Pet Travel Rules Method 2026: CDC, USDA and Airline Sources';
const description = 'How the pet travel figures are built in 2026: CDC dog import rules, USDA APHIS destination pages and fees, and five airlines read on their pages and contracts.';
const dl = K.feeOr('delta', 'us');
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[webPageSchema({ name: 'How the figures are built', description, path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'How the figures are built', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'How the figures are built' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>How the pet travel figures are built</h1>
    <p><strong>Every fee and rule on this site was read on the document of the body that sets it: the airline for its fee and carrier, the CDC for a dog entering the United States, USDA APHIS for what a foreign country asks. Nothing is estimated; a figure we could not read is not shown.</strong></p>
    <p>{VALUE}</p>
    <h2>1. Airline fees and carriers</h2>
    <p>Five airlines were read on {K.day(K.P.retrieved_at)}: Delta on its <Fragment set:html={src('delta_pets', 'pet travel page')} />, American on its <Fragment set:html={src('aa_pets', 'pets page')} />, Southwest in its <Fragment set:html={src('wn_coc', 'contract of carriage of November 6, 2026')} /> and its <Fragment set:html={src('wn_fees', 'fee page')} />, Alaska in its <Fragment set:html={src('as_coc', 'contract of carriage of August 25, 2026')} /> and <Fragment set:html={src('as_dogs', 'its newsroom guide of August 26, 2026')} />, Frontier on its <Fragment set:html={src('f9_faq', 'pet FAQ')} /> and <Fragment set:html={src('f9_fees', 'fee page')} />. The fee of a route is shown only when the airline writes it for that route; a refusal is shown only when the airline writes it. Everything else reads “not published”. </p>
    <p set:html={others()} />
    <p>For the carrier checker, the three sides you enter are sorted from largest to smallest and compared with the airline’s maximum sorted the same way, so a carrier entered as 11 x 18 x 11 is read like 18 x 11 x 11. Weight is checked only where the airline publishes a limit: American, {K.A('american').maxLb} pounds for the pet and the carrier.</p>
    <h2>2. Entry into the United States</h2>
    <p>The CDC rules come from its <Fragment set:html={src('cdc_faq', 'FAQ on dog importations')} />, its <Fragment set:html={src('cdc_form', 'Dog Import Form instructions')} />, its <Fragment set:html={src('cdc_highrisk', 'list of high-risk countries')} /> ({K.HR.length} entries, kept as published) and its <Fragment set:html={src('cdc_acf', 'list of animal care facilities')} />. The checker puts a dog in one of the CDC’s four cases from two answers: was it in a high-risk country in the last six months, and where was it vaccinated.</p>
    <h2>3. Destinations and USDA fees</h2>
    <p>Each destination’s rules come from its USDA APHIS page, dated on the page: Mexico, Canada, France for the European Union, Great Britain, Japan, and the page for Finland, Malta, Ireland and Norway. The endorsement fees are those of the <Fragment set:html={src('aphis_fees', 'APHIS schedule')} />. The planner counts days before the flight; it does not know your pet’s history, which only your veterinarian’s records show.</p>
    <h2>4. A worked example</h2>
    <p>The example case of the site is a small dog flying Delta in the cabin, round trip within the mainland US, in a soft carrier of {K.in([...K.EX.dims])} weighing {K.EX.lb} pounds with the dog. Delta charges {K.usd(dl)} each way, so {K.usd(dl * 2)} for the round trip. The carrier is within the size Delta recommends, within American’s soft maximum and Frontier’s, and too high for Alaska’s soft limit of {K.in(K.A('alaska').carrier!.soft!)}.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={table(['Step', 'Value'], [['Delta fee, one way, within the US', K.usd(dl)], ['Legs', '2'], ['Airline fees', K.usd(dl * 2)], ['USDA endorsement (not needed within the US)', '$0'], ['CDC Dog Import Form (no trip abroad)', 'not needed']], 'The example case, step by step', ['l', 'r'])} />
    <h2>5. Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Airlines change fees and rules without notice; the booking screen and the agent at the counter decide.</li>
      <li>Under-seat space varies by aircraft: a carrier within the published maximum can still be refused.</li>
      <li>No veterinary information: vaccines, tests and doses appear only as dates and documents the rules require.</li>
      <li>Hawaii’s state entry rules, pet shipper prices and vet prices are not covered.</li>
      <li>Nothing here is veterinary, legal or travel advice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Corrections: <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
